---
title: 'Installation'
description: 'Learn how to install AG Charts and add $framework charts and $framework graphs to your application. Supports bundled and non-bundled projects. Upgrade to Enterprise for additional features.'
---

{% if isFramework("javascript") %}

AG Charts is available for download from NPM, CDN or as a direct download, however, we strongly recommend using either NPM or CDN. When using NPM, you need to import the package and register the modules you want to use.

## NPM Installation

{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("react", "angular", "vue") %}

AG Charts is available for download from NPM & Yarn. Once installed, you just need to import the package.

## Installation

{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("react") %}
Install the `ag-charts-react` package, which also installs `ag-charts-community`:

{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("angular") %}
Install the `ag-charts-angular` package, which also installs `ag-charts-community`:

{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("vue") %}
Install the `ag-charts-vue3` package, which also installs `ag-charts-community`:

{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("javascript") %}
Install the `ag-charts-community` package:

{% /if %}

{% tabs omitFromOverview=true snippetTabs=true %}
{% tabItem id="js-npm" label="NPM" %}

{% if isFramework("react") %}

```bash
npm install ag-charts-react
```

{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("angular") %}

```bash
npm install ag-charts-angular
```

{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("vue") %}

```bash
npm install ag-charts-vue3
```

{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("javascript") %}

```bash
npm install ag-charts-community
```

{% /if %}

{% /tabItem %}
{% tabItem id="js-yarn" label="Yarn" %}
{% if isFramework("react") %}

```bash
yarn add ag-charts-react
```

{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("angular") %}

```bash
yarn add ag-charts-angular
```

{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("vue") %}

```bash
yarn add ag-charts-vue3
```

{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("javascript") %}

```bash
yarn add ag-charts-community
```

{% /if %}
{% /tabItem %}
{% /tabs %}

To use AG Charts Enterprise features, install the `ag-charts-enterprise` package:

{% tabs omitFromOverview=true snippetTabs=true %}
{% tabItem id="js-npm" label="NPM" %}

```bash
npm install ag-charts-enterprise
```

{% /tabItem %}
{% tabItem id="js-yarn" label="Yarn" %}

```bash
yarn add ag-charts-enterprise
```

{% /tabItem %}
{% /tabs %}

{% note %}
You can test AG Charts Enterprise locally without a licence. To test in production, access support and remove the watermark & console warnings, [request a trial licence](./community-vs-enterprise/#request-an-enterprise-bundle-trial-licence).
{% /note %}

### Registering Modules

Register the `AllCommunityModule` to access all Community features:

```js
import { AllCommunityModule, ModuleRegistry } from 'ag-charts-community';

// Register all Community features
ModuleRegistry.registerModules([AllCommunityModule]);
```

Register the `AllEnterpriseBundle` to access all Community and Enterprise features:

```js
import { AllEnterpriseModule, ModuleRegistry } from 'ag-charts-enterprise';

// Register all Community and Enterprise features
ModuleRegistry.registerModules([AllEnterpriseModule]);
```

{% note %}
To minimize bundle size, only register the modules you want to use. See the [Selecting Modules](./module-registry/#selecting-modules) docs for more information.
{% /note %}

{% if isFramework("react", "angular", "vue") %}

## Importing

{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("javascript") %}

### Importing

{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("react") %}
Import the `AgCharts` component from the `ag-charts-react` package:

```js
import { AgCharts } from 'ag-charts-react';
```

{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("angular") %}
Import the `AgCharts` component from the `ag-charts-angular` package:

```js
import { AgCharts } from 'ag-charts-angular';
```

{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("vue") %}
Import the `AgCharts` component from the `ag-charts-vue3` package:

```js
import { AgCharts } from 'ag-charts-vue3';
```

{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("javascript") %}
To use AG Charts Community features, import them from the `ag-charts-community` package, e.g:

```js
import { AgCharts } from 'ag-charts-community';
```

{% /if %}

To use AG Charts Enterprise features, import the `ag-charts-enterprise` package:

```js
import 'ag-charts-enterprise';
```

See the [Installing Enterprise Licence Key](./license-install/) docs for more information on how to install your Enterprise or [Trial](./community-vs-enterprise/#request-an-enterprise-bundle-trial-licence) licence key.

{% if isFramework("react", "angular", "vue") %}

## Accessing AG Charts

{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("javascript") %}

### Accessing AG Charts

{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("react") %}

To use AG Charts in your React application, return the `AgCharts` component with your chart options:

```tsx format="reactHooks"
const MyChart = () => {
    // Define chart options; mutating this object will cause the chart to update
    const [chartOptions, setChartOptions] = useState({
        /*...*/
    });

    // Return the AgCharts component with the chart options
    return <AgCharts options={chartOptions} />;
};
```

{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("angular") %}

To use AG Charts in your Angular application, return the `ag-charts` component with your chart options:

```ts
@Component({
    selector: 'app-root',
    standalone: true,
    imports: [AgCharts],
    template: `<ag-charts style="height: 100%" [options]="chartOptions"> </ag-charts>`,
})
export class AppComponent {
    // Chart Options
    public chartOptions: AgChartOptions;
    constructor() {
        this.chartOptions = {
            /*...*/
        };
    }
}
```

{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("vue") %}
To use AG Charts in your Vue application, return the `ag-charts` component with your chart options:

```html
<template>
    <!-- The AG Charts component with chartsOptions as an attribute -->
    <ag-charts :options="options"> </ag-charts>
</template>

<script>
    setup() {
      return {
        ref<AgChartOptions>({/*...*/}),
      };
    },
</script>
```

{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("javascript") %}

To use AG Charts in your JavaScript application, use the `create` API to create a chart with your chart options:

```js format="snippet"
// Chart Options
const options = {
    /*...*/
};

// Create Chart
const chart = AgCharts.create(options);
```

{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("javascript") %}

## CDN Installation

To install AG Charts Community, include the following script tags in your HTML file:

```html
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/ag-charts-community@11.1.0/dist/umd/ag-charts-community.min.js"></script>
```

To install AG Charts Enterprise, include the following script tags in your HTML file:

```html
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/ag-charts-enterprise@11.1.0/dist/umd/ag-charts-enterprise.min.js"></script>
```

Once installed, you can then access AG Charts via the `agCharts.AgCharts` global variable. See the [Quick Start](./quick-start/) for more information.

## Download

If your project does not use a package manager and you don't want to refer to AG Charts from CDN, you can download AG Charts' source files and keep them in your project structure.

{% warning %}
Downloading AG Charts makes upgrading more complex and prone to errors. We recommend using AG Charts from an NPM/Yarn package or from CDN.
{% /warning %}

{% tabs %}
{% tabItem id="community" label="Community" %}
You can download AG Charts Community from the {% link href="https://github.com/ag-grid/ag-charts/releases/download/r11.1.0/ag-charts-community.tgz" %}GitHub Repository{% /link %}.
{% /tabItem %}
{% tabItem id="enterprise" label="Enterprise" %}
You can download AG Charts Enterprise from the {% link href="https://github.com/ag-grid/ag-charts/releases/download/r11.1.0/ag-charts-enterprise.tgz" %}GitHub Repository{% /link %}.
{% /tabItem %}
{% /tabs %}

After downloading the bundles, you can refer to the files in the same way as you would from CDN. See the [Quick Start](./quick-start/) for more information.

{% /if %}
